<</A 2695 0 R /Alt(\r\nGiven:\rTotal Samples = 100\rTrue Positives \(TP\) = 80 \(The model correctly predicted 80 genes as genes\)\rFalse Positives \(FP\) = 20 \(The model incorrectly predicted 20 non-genes as genes\)\rFalse Negatives \(FN\) = 10 \(The model incorrectly predicted 10 genes as non-genes\)\rTrue Negatives \(TN\) = 90 \(The model correctly predicted 90 non-genes as non-genes\)\r\r1. Accuracy\rAccuracy is the proportion of correct predictions \(both True Positives \(TP\) and True Negatives \(TN\)\) out of all predictions \(TP + TN + FP + FN\).\rAccuracy equals numerator , TP plus TN end numerator , over denominator , TP plus TN plus FP plus FN end denominator \rSubstitute the values:\rAccuracy equals numerator , 80 plus 90 end numerator , over denominator , 80 plus 90 plus 20 plus 10 end denominator , equals 170 over 200 equals 0.85\rAnswer: Accuracy = 0.85 or 85%\r\r)/K[ 1]/P 2693 0 R /Pg 2151 0 R /S/Formula/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
