<</A 2701 0 R /Alt(\r\n2. Precision\rPrecision is the proportion of correctly predicted positive instances \(True Positives\) out of all predicted positives \(True Positives + False Positives\).\rPrecision equals TP over denominator , TP plus FP end denominator \rSubstitute the values:\rPrecision equals 80 over denominator , 80 plus 20 end denominator , equals 80 over 100 equals 0.8\rAnswer: Precision = 0.8 or 80%\r\r3. Recall \(Sensitivity\)\rRecall is the proportion of correctly predicted positive instances \(True Positives\) out of all actual positives \(True Positives + False Negatives\).\rRecall equals TP over denominator , TP plus FN end denominator \rSubstitute the values:\rRecall equals 80 over denominator , 80 plus 10 end denominator , equals 80 over 90 equals 0.89\rAnswer: Recall = 0.89 or 89%\r\r)/K[ 1]/P 2699 0 R /Pg 2152 0 R /S/Formula/Type/StructElem>>
