<</A 2707 0 R /Alt(\r\n4. F1 Score\rThe F1 Score is the harmonic mean of precision and recall. It provides a balance between the two.\rF1 Score equals 2 times numerator , Precision times Recall end numerator , over denominator , Precision plus Recall end denominator \rSubstitute the values:\rF1 Score equals 2 times numerator , 0.8 times 0.89 end numerator , over denominator , 0.8 plus 0.89 end denominator , equals 2 times 0.712 over 1.69 equals 1.424 over 1.69 almost equal to 0.84\rAnswer: F1 Score = 0.84 or 84%\r5. Specificity, also known as the True Negative Rate \(TNR\), is the proportion of correctly predicted negative instances \(True Negatives\) out of all actual negative instances \(True Negatives + False Positives\).\rFormula for Specificity:\rSpecificity equals TN over denominator , TN plus FP end denominator \rTrue Negatives \(TN\) = 90\rFalse Positives \(FP\) = 20\rCalculation:\rSpecificity equals 90 over denominator , 90 plus 20 end denominator , equals 90 over 110 equals 0.8181\r\r)/K[ 1]/P 2705 0 R /Pg 2153 0 R /S/Formula/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
